From 44be978ed7163bc2e560460ddb285efb7fc2b8b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anders Kaseorg <andersk@mit.edu>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:54:24 +0000
Subject: don't send firmware commands for BIP keys

mac80211 does BIP in software, but mwl_mac80211_set_key() still sent
UPDATE_ENCRYPTION with ENCR_TYPE_DISABLE for the BSS address when the
IGTK was installed, right after the GTK had set it to AES. Only then
did mwl_fwcmd_encryption_set_cmd_info() return 1 to fall back to
software.

With PMF, which WPA3 requires, this breaks group addressed traffic
from the AP: on a WRT3200ACM (88W8964), a wireless client's ARP
request for another wireless client is never answered (also reported
for the 88W8864 in #362).

Return 1 for AES_CMAC before talking to the firmware at all.

Based on neheb/mwlwifi commit cd43e4f by Rosen Penev.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anders Kaseorg <andersk@mit.edu>
---
 mac80211.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -522,6 +522,14 @@ static int mwl_mac80211_set_key(struct i
 	mwl_vif = mwl_dev_get_vif(vif);
 	addr = sta ? sta->addr : vif->addr;
 
+	/* mac80211 does BIP in software. Don't tell the firmware anything
+	 * about the IGTK: an UPDATE_ENCRYPTION with ENCR_TYPE_DISABLE for
+	 * the BSS address would override the encryption type set for the
+	 * GTK, and break group addressed traffic.
+	 */
+	if (key->cipher == WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_AES_CMAC)
+		return 1;
+
 	if (cmd_param == SET_KEY) {
 		if ((key->cipher == WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_WEP40) ||
 		    (key->cipher == WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_WEP104)) {
